## Real image build passed; CPU acceptance stopped

[CPU release candidate run 34321790686](https://github.com/saidi19/lumi-model/actions/runs/34321790686),
job `102369854047`, failed once at **cpu_acceptance**, after **55 seconds** of
builder runtime. The scoped report requires that these earlier stages returned
success before reaching this stage:

- Same-commit tracked-source snapshot: **465 files / 11,567,702 bytes**.
- Pinned base inspection and inventory: **2375 files / 82,518,542 bytes**;
  base distribution metadata contains only pip **25.0.1**.
- All **34 exact wheels / 248,715,637 bytes** passed size and SHA-256 checks.
- Offline, binary-only, hash-locked image build and `pip check` completed.
- Final image-ID container creation and nonroot/read-only/network-none,
  no-host-software-bind/device inspection passed.

These are program-order claims supported by the reached stage and retained
control files, not an invented per-stage success transcript. The v1 failed
report does not retain the built image ID; do not invent one. The immutable
image was built, but it is **not an accepted release**, and no image archive was
uploaded. The workflow skipped its accepted-image upload step. There was no
second container acceptance start, CI rerun, promotion or registry push.

The exact retained probe failure is:

```
probe_stage = worker_run
fixture_stage = ledger
child_stage = run
code = probe_failed
```

`child_stage=run` spans the entire `WorkerRun.run()` call. It does not establish
which component failed, whether the input-origin witness was reached, or how
many optimizer steps occurred. It is not evidence of corrupt data, an invalid
model, a GPU issue, or a proven OverlayFS bug. Existing rejection checks remain
unchanged. `real_sft_execution_permitted=false` and `production_eligible=false`.

The failed image's generated temporary files were not added to the immutable
image. The exact owned worker container was retired: no cleanup-failed flag was
reported, and the final cleanup path completed. Do not infer successful fixture
cleanup counters from a failed probe.

