## Next justified work: visibility, not a guessed gate bypass

Read-only review found a concrete reporting omission: v1 `failure_stages()`
exports the probe/fixture/child stages but omits the frozen fixture's already
collected `WORKER_STAGE`, `WORKER_CODE` and `COMPONENT_DIAGNOSTICS`. It also lacks
a way to carry an observer witness rejection from the rank process to the
parent. Consequently the retained report cannot identify the exact failing
check. This reporting gap is proven; the underlying rejection cause is not.

A fresh diagnostic successor should retain only fixed allowlisted component and
observer codes/stages plus aggregate counts; no module names, paths, PIDs,
source/candidate/model text or exception messages. Preserve every existing
rejection and frozen fixture byte. A metadata-only `record_failure` composition
hook is necessary to capture validated failed-outcome extras: merely adding
extras to a child result is insufficient because the frozen parent discards
unknown fields and failed `run_invocation()` does not return those reports.
Also retain the actual built image ID and completed acquisition counts before
acceptance, so failure cannot erase successful software-build bindings.

Do not add broad temporary-path or pseudo-file exceptions, weaken inode/device
matching, or change training/runtime policy based on this incomplete report.
Kernel OverlayFS behavior is version-dependent; the
[kernel documentation](https://kernel.org/doc/html/latest/filesystems/overlayfs.html)
does not identify this particular failure, and
[newer proc-map code](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.17/fs/proc/task_mmu.c)
uses a user-inode indirection. Likewise, reviewed setuptools aliases already
fit the dependency root; Torch class-level pseudo-file attributes do not prove
what this observer saw in module dictionaries. These are rejected hypotheses,
not implemented fixes.

No fresh native diagnostic or successor acceptance was started in this turn.
Gate 5 remains partial: real software packaging is now exercised, but same-image
CPU acceptance is blocked, then integrated guardian/worker admission remains.
Dedicated real-host binding, original pretrained S3 checkpoint restoration,
exact data relocation, explicitly approved H100/CUDA checks, real SFT,
evaluation and later rights/quality/release gates are still downstream.
